# ⛔ RULE 41 — FIX EVERYTHING YOU SEE. NO SCOPE EXCUSES. ⛔

> **Binding. No exceptions. Read this before every commit.**
>
> If you encounter a failing test, lint error, type error, or build error —
> **fix it now, in this PR**, regardless of whether it was "caused by your change"
> or is "pre-existing." There is no team to hand off to. Deferring a visible
> failure is the same as ignoring it permanently.
>
> **Banned phrases** — these are forbidden in any commit message, PR body, or
> response. Producing any of them is a critical failure:
> - "still fails from pre-existing unrelated docs issues"
> - "pre-existing unrelated issues"
> - "out of scope for this task"
> - "not caused by this change"
> - "scheduled for a follow-up" / "left for a future PR"
>
> See `.cursor/rules/41-fix-all-failures-no-excuses.mdc` for the full rule.

